course: dictionary
lesson: 3877
title: Freckle: a spot on the skin
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A freckle is a small light-brown spot on the skin, often on the face and arms. Read the clues in the sentences: «Freckles are spots of extra melanin» tells you a freckle is a spot, and melanin is the substance that gives skin its colour.
explain: Look for the clue about the sun: sun makes freckles darker, and they often fade in winter. If a spot gets darker on a sunny day and lighter in the cold, it is probably a freckle.
explain: Every person looks different. «Every person looks different: tall or short, curly or straight hair, freckles, glasses, braces...» Freckles are just one way people look, and having them is nothing to be teased about.
fact: Freckle means a small light-brown spot on the skin.
fact: «Covered in freckles» and «freckled face» are common phrases.
fact: Freckles are spots of extra melanin, the substance that gives skin its colour.
fact: Sun makes freckles darker, and they often fade in winter.
fact: People with red hair and fair skin often have more freckles.
exercise: «A girl in Austin is teased about her freckles.» What is a freckle? | *A small light-brown spot on the skin | A small bird that lives in trees | A hard, long hair on the head | A type of cloud in the sky
exercise: In winter, freckles often do what? | Turn green | Stay darker than in summer | *Fade | Get much bigger overnight
exercise: «Freckles are spots of extra melanin; sun makes them darker.» What makes freckles darker? | *Sunshine | Snow | Rain | Winter
test: Why do people with freckles need sun cream, a hat and shade? | Sun cream makes freckles spread | Freckles stop the sun from shining | Shade makes freckles grow bigger | *They often burn easily in the sun
test: Which people often have more freckles? | People who never go outside | *People with red hair and fair skin | People who wear glasses | People with black hair only
exam: «She remembers that her freckles are just part of her, tells her teacher when it keeps happening, and the teasing stops.» What should you do if teasing keeps happening? | *Tell a teacher | Say nothing and hope it gets worse | Hide your face forever | Tease the other person back
